xfce4-focus-plugin (0.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the dropdown arrow being invisible when the plugin is added to
    a vertical panel: the button row now re-orients itself (and swaps
    the arrow glyph) in response to the panel's own orientation.
  * Mark the plugin unique (X-XFCE-Unique=true) so the panel only
    allows one instance of it across all panels at once, instead of
    letting independent instances fight over the same D-Bus inhibit
    and Do Not Disturb setting.
  * Fix Do Not Disturb staying on forever if the plugin is removed
    from the panel while active (FocusDnd's dispose now turns it back
    off, mirroring what FocusInhibit's dispose already did for Stay
    Awake).
  * Fix a use-after-free crash on plugin teardown: FocusDnd was
    unreffing the shared, process-wide xfconf channel object returned
    by xfconf_channel_get() as if it owned a reference to it, which
    could take down xfconf for the rest of the panel process (or crash
    outright) instead of just releasing its own signal handler.
  * Redraw the "Add New Items" / Panel Preferences icon with bolder,
    thicker linework traced from the same reference artwork as the
    panel button's own icon -- the previous thin strokes collapsed
    into an unrecognizable blob at the small size those dialogs use.
  * Fix the panel icon going stale (wrong colors, sometimes invisible)
    after a live light/dark theme switch, until something else (e.g.
    clicking the button) happened to redraw it. Both hand-recolored
    icons (the main eye and the dropdown's "no bell" glyph) now listen
    for GTK's own style-updated signal and re-render immediately.
  * Fix the active-state icon showing the current GTK theme's default
    checked-button background (a visibly mismatched box on light
    themes) behind the eye -- the toggle button is now fully flattened
    in every state, letting only the icon convey whether Focus mode is
    active.

 -- Rodrigo <rodrigo@ffr.cl>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:19:43 -0300

xfce4-focus-plugin (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Re-derive the main button's eye icons from new reference artwork
    (eye3.png/eye4.png) using the same alpha-from-luminance extraction
    as before. Also fixes a transcription error found while verifying
    this build: one byte of the previous "open" icon's embedded PNG
    data didn't match its source file, silently corrupting that icon.

 -- Rodrigo <rodrigo@ffr.cl>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:11:43 -0300

xfce4-focus-plugin (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the main button's hand-drawn eye icons with ones derived
    directly from the user-supplied eye1.png/eye2.png reference
    artwork: each pixel's inverted luminance becomes an alpha channel
    (the originals are opaque, not transparent), embedded as small
    base64 PNGs and recolored at render time to the current foreground
    color, so they still adapt to light/dark panel themes despite
    starting from fixed-color raster art. Verified end-to-end with a
    standalone render at 16/22/32px before shipping.

 -- Rodrigo <rodrigo@ffr.cl>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:49:54 -0300

